Author: QIU023 <yiqiaoqiu@hotmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 16 21:53:36 2026 +0000

    torchtitan engine: context parallel through the model's own preprocessing
    
    The engine's CP path was written against prepare_context_parallel_input,
    which torchtitan no longer exports, and against a model that ran CP inside
    its modules. On the current tree the model owns its CP preprocessing:
    apply ContextParallelTransform to the trainer config at construction (the
    all-gather-KV backend for flex attention, the KDA routing counterpart where
    the tree has one), hand preprocess_inputs the folded [T] stream with the
    global positions and take back this rank's inputs, masks and routing. The
    shards are contiguous and rank-ordered, so the logits gather back in order;
    its backward takes this rank's slice unscaled, as the tp gather does, since
    every cp rank computes the same full loss and FSDP reduces over dp_shard x
    cp. Packed multi-document micro-batches no longer need one sequence each.
    The engine keeps the trainer's ParallelDims instead of a second mesh, and
    probes the folded-stream contract on the model instead of on its name.

